# Rootwork TypeScript starter

This repository is a **framework-agnostic TypeScript repository template**, not an application starter.

## What belongs here

Only boring setup we would want in nearly every new TypeScript repo:

- pnpm + lockfile pinning
- strict TypeScript (typecheck only)
- Biome for format / lint / imports
- Conventional Commits, commitlint, Husky `commit-msg`
- semantic-release for GitHub Releases (not npm by default)
- minimal CI

## What does not belong here

Do **not** add unless a concrete downstream project needs it (and usually not in this template at all):

- App frameworks (React, Next, Astro, etc.)
- Test runners, bundlers, Docker, databases
- ESLint, Prettier, lint-staged, Commitizen, Changesets
- Application dependencies or feature code beyond a trivial `src/` placeholder

## Decision test

Before adding anything, ask: “Would we want this in almost every new TypeScript repository?”

If no, leave it out. Prefer small, explicit config over clever abstraction.

## Creating new repos from this template

Agent-driven creation uses the personal Cursor command `/new-ts-repo` (not defined in this repo). Keep this template focused on repository-level conventions only.
